---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import data from "../../data/processed/ecosystem.json";
import { href, hours, date } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="Ecosystem reconnaissance">
  <div class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Research / Public GitHub evidence</div>
    <h1>Signals, with their context.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      An intentionally small sample of developer-facing repositories. No
      community scores. No maintainer rankings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collected {date(data.collectedAt)} UTC · Created-item cohort:{" "}
      {date(data.window.start)}–{date(data.window.end)}. Counts include
      automation; they do not measure unique people or outside contributions.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Activity in the observation window</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <caption>
          Four indicators; duration and response are explicitly simplified
          proxies.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Repository</th>
            <th scope="col">New issues</th>
            <th scope="col">New PRs</th>
            <th scope="col">PR closure proxy</th>
            <th scope="col">First-comment response proxy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.repositories.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                <a href={r.url}>{r.name.replace("mapbox/", "")}</a>
              </th>
              <td>{r.metrics.issuesOpened}</td>
              <td>{r.metrics.prsOpened}</td>
              <td>
                {hours(r.metrics.medianPrCloseHours)}
                <small>{r.metrics.closedPrs} closed PRs</small>
              </td>
              <td>
                {hours(r.metrics.medianSampleResponseHours)}
                <small>
                  {r.metrics.respondedSample}/{r.metrics.responseSampleSize}{" "}
                  sampled issues have an eligible comment
                </small>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Read the denominators.</strong> Closure includes merged and
      unmerged PRs created in the window and closed by its end; open PRs are
      censored. Response medians exclude unanswered issues and include only
      non-author, non-Bot issue comments. Draw’s 0/2 sample means no eligible
      observed response, not zero-hour response. Geocoder has no new issues to
      sample. <a href={href("methodology")}>Definitions and bias →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="two">
    <div>
      <h2>What kind of activity is visible?</h2>
      <p>
        Counts show the balance of new issues and PRs inside each repository’s
        own cohort. They cannot explain who participates or why. Bars show the
        share of items that are PRs, not community health.
      </p>
      {data.repositories.map((r) => {
        const total = r.metrics.issuesOpened + r.metrics.prsOpened;
        return (
          <div style="margin-bottom:20px">
            <span class="muted">
              {r.name} · {r.metrics.prsOpened}/{total} items are PRs
            </span>
            <div
              class="bar"
              role="img"
              aria-label={`${r.metrics.prsOpened} of ${total} items are pull requests`}
            >
              <span
                style={`width:${total ? (r.metrics.prsOpened / total) * 100 : 0}%`}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        );
      })}
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <span class="badge">Unavailable</span>
      <h3>A trend needs more than one snapshot</h3>
      <p>
        Historical comparisons are not shown. There is one collected window, no
        reliable baseline, and no contributor identity history.
      </p>
      <p>
        New contributors, concentration, review duration, and newcomer success
        remain unavailable. GitHub data alone cannot measure belonging, private
        support, or developer satisfaction.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={href("opportunities")}>
        Questions worth testing →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="pathways">
    <h2>Repository purpose & contribution pathways</h2>
    <p>
      File presence is a discoverability check, not a measure of documentation
      quality. Missing files may be replaced by README guidance or
      organization-level defaults. Public visibility does not imply an
      open-source license or unrestricted outside contribution.
    </p>
    {data.repositories.map((r) => (
      <details open>
        <summary>
          {r.name} · {r.archived ? "Archived" : "Unarchived"} · last push{" "}
          {date(r.pushedAt)}
        </summary>
        <p>{r.description}</p>
        <p>
          <strong>License:</strong>{" "}
          {r.license === "NOASSERTION"
            ? "GitHub could not assign a standard SPDX license. GL JS uses Mapbox-specific terms; inspect LICENSE.txt before reuse."
            : r.license}{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href={`${r.url}/blob/${r.branch}/${r.docs.LICENSE[0]}`}>
            Read license ↗
          </a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Contribution entry:</strong>{" "}
          {r.docs.CONTRIBUTING.length ? (
            <a href={`${r.url}/blob/${r.branch}/${r.docs.CONTRIBUTING[0]}`}>
              CONTRIBUTING guidance ↗
            </a>
          ) : (
            <a href={`${r.url}#developing-and-testing`}>
              README development & custom modes ↗
            </a>
          )}
          .{" "}
          {r.name.endsWith("mapbox-gl-js")
            ? "The guide describes development and tests, plus an internal import and Copybara sync workflow: accepted public PRs may appear Closed rather than Merged. Closure cannot be interpreted as rejection."
            : r.name.endsWith("mapbox-gl-draw")
              ? "The README invites pull requests and describes development/testing; no standalone CONTRIBUTING file was found."
              : "The contribution guide provides a development and testing entry point; confirm issue scope before proposing changes."}
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          No dedicated SUPPORT or CODE_OF_CONDUCT filename found in this
          repository tree. Organization defaults and README channels were not
          exhaustively audited. Tree truncated: {String(r.treeTruncated)}.
        </p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </section>
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Candidate excluded:</strong>{" "}
    {data.candidates.map((c) => (
      <p>
        {c.name}: {c.status}{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.mapbox.com/mapbox-search-js/">
          Public Search JS documentation ↗
        </a>{" "}
        is a product reference, not evidence of a public contribution
        repository.
      </p>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>
    <a href={href("data/github.json")}>Download normalized evidence JSON ↗</a> ·{" "}
    <a href={href("data/ecosystem.json")}>Download presentation snapshot ↗</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
